- `draw_text().py` 

# Summary

- A `Radiobutton` allows for one choice of several possible options (mutually exclusive)
  - Can use `IntVar` to get and select default for selected `Radiobutton`
- A `Checkbutton` allows for multiple choice among several possible options (not mutually exclusive)
- A `Listbox` displays textual list, and can be used for single or multiple choice
  - Can be more flexible than radio buttons or list boxes, can build dynamically
  - Adding scrollbars to `tkinter` elements can be a bit tricky...
- The `Canvas` widget provides a canvas that you can draw arbitrary geometric shapes on
  - Methods with support for lines, rectangles, ovals, polygons, text on the canvas 


